# Screening A[i]gent
AI-powered application review and candidate evaluation engine.

Screening A[i]gent gives every resume a structured, objective, and consistent deep-dive in seconds. It replaces 6-second scans and inconsistent manual screening with a rubric-driven, auditable evaluation layer that surfaces hidden talent and improves downstream funnel quality.

---

## 1. Overview
Inbound applications are noisy. Recruiters spend significant time manually verifying experience, tenure, education, and required skills. Strong candidates often get overlooked due to volume and inconsistency.

Screening A[i]gent transforms early-stage evaluation by converting resumes and job descriptions into structured intelligence.

**Key benefits:**
- Faster, more consistent screening
- High-potential candidates surfaced early
- Cleaner ATS data for analytics
- Reduced screening bias
- Improved recruiter focus and speed

---

## 2. What Screening A[i]gent Does

### Core Capabilities
- AI-powered resume analysis and experience verification
- Competitor and employer lookup with industry adjacency scoring
- Rubric scoring based on job description and must-have criteria
- Fit evaluation (Match / Partial / Mismatch) with justification
- Tenure stability and risk detection
- Structured “Ask Next” prompts for recruiter phone screens
- Advance recommendation with required human review
- ATS-ready structured output for reporting and downstream agents

Screening A[i]gent performs the heavy lifting so recruiters can focus on judgment, not data gathering.

---

## 3. How It Works

### 3.1 Inputs
- Job description
- Hiring manager requirements
- Resume or structured application data
- Competitor index
- Rubric templates

### 3.2 Processing Pipeline
1. Convert job description into a rubric
2. Parse and normalize resume data
3. Identify and classify employers and competitor adjacency
4. Score experience, tenure, education, and must-haves
5. Evaluate fit and detect risk indicators
6. Generate structured summary and recommendation
7. Require human approval or override with notes
8. Push structured output to ATS fields

---

## 4. Rubric Framework

### Scoring Categories
| Category | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Experience | Relevancy, depth, seniority alignment, years of experience |
| Tenure | Stability indicators, average tenure, patterns and gaps |
| Education | Required vs preferred credentials |
| Competitor Fit | Employer pedigree and industry adjacency |
| Skills Match | Must-have tools and domain expertise |
| Soft Signals | Writing clarity, detail, and follow-through |

Rubrics convert subjective signals into objective and explainable evaluation criteria.

---

## 5. Output

### Candidate Summary Card Includes:
- Fit score and rubric category scores
- Competitor match classification
- Tenure and stability indicators
- Matches vs mismatches
- Flags and risks
- Recommendation for next steps

### Recommendation Types
- Advance
- Recommend HM Review
- Do Not Advance (with reasons)

### Human Review Layer
All recommendations require recruiter approval or override, ensuring:
- Auditability
- Fairness governance
- Consistent decision rationale

---

## 6. Why It Matters
- Reduces screening time from 15 minutes to 60–90 seconds
- Saves 50–75 recruiter hours per 300 applications
- Improves pipeline quality and reduces bias
- Produces clean, structured data for reporting
- Provides consistent hiring manager alignment
- Reduces operational drag while increasing throughput

---

## 7. Integration

### Upstream Inputs
- Job description
- Hiring manager rubric
- Competitor index
- Resume parsing system

### Downstream Outputs
- ATS structured fields
- Workflow A[i]gent (scheduling automation triggers)
- Metrics A[i]gent (stage conversions, quality metrics)

### Shared Layer
- Metrics Dictionary for unified analytics and definitions

---

## 8. Example Use Cases
- High-potential, nontraditional candidates are surfaced
- Recruiters eliminate repetitive manual verification
- Hiring managers receive structured, consistent signals
- Funnel reporting becomes reliable and comparable
- Overrides provide transparency and bias governance

